    {
      "id": "122",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 122,
        "relationship_type": "synonym",
        "body": "Both もう and すでに express the idea of 'already.' The difference is their level of formality and tone. While もう is commonly used in everyday conversation and can have a personal or emotional nuance, すでに is more objective and found primarily in writing or formal speech. もう can also be used alone as an expression of exasperation or frustration, while すでに cannot.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 42,
          "slug": "もう",
